                <pb facs="0625" n="619" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg619"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase of telegram from Consul Cusack-Smith,
                        Samoa, March 22, 1894, received March 31.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Hostilities have been in progress since the 10th instant. Hitherto the Government
                    troops have been successful. The foreign consuls have undertaken to mediate. An
                    armistice has just been proclaimed and a satisfactory peace is expected to
                    follow. It is not at all necessary to send a man-of-war to Samoa.</p>
            </div>
